.TH QUANUX-ARENA 6 "FEBRUARY 2026" "QuanuX Biological Sovereignty" "QuanuX System Manual"
.SH NAME
quanux-arena \- The Training Cortex (Simulated Survival / Thymus)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quanux-spreader --sim
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBquanux-arena\fR represents Section 6 (Games/Simulation) of the QuanuX manual array, but in the Biological Sovereignty model, it is the \fBThymus\fR. 

It is the Neural Sandbox where the Strategy Nucleus is exposed to Synthetic Pathogens to ensure its biological fitness before it is allowed to enter the live network fluid. "Play" is the highest form of evolutionary preparation.
.SH EVOLUTION VIA SYNTHETIC ENTROPY
When the metabolic enzyme (\fBquanux-spreader(1)\fR) is executed with the \fB--sim\fR flag, it operates entirely within the Arena. The Arena deliberately injects \fBSynthetic Entropy\fR into the receptors to calculate a Survival Fitness Score.

This entropy mimics real-world Institutional Pathogens:
.IP \[ci] 3
.B Latency Jitter:
Artificial delays are injected across the NATS synapses, testing if the Nucleus can calculate stale alphas without violating risk Interlocks.
.IP \[ci] 3
.B Order-Book Poisoning:
Phantom depth forces the engine to recalculate its mass.
.IP \[ci] 3
.B Liquidity Gaps:
Testing the \fBSTATE_HEDGE\fR reflexes when opposing volume vanishes.
.SH THE LAW OF MITOSIS INTEGRITY
The single most critical law of the Arena is \fBMitosis Integrity\fR (Sim-Live Parity). The Nucleus evaluated in the Arena must be the exact identical genetic sequence (SHA-256 binary hash) that is deployed to the live ingestion port.

Because the Arena uses the exact same \fBquanux-shm(4)\fR and \fBquanux-vault(5)\fR organelles as production, there is no "simulation drift." The cell's simulated mitosis perfectly replicates its live-fire behavior down to the physical L3 cache line.
.SH THE INVARIANT
A strategy that fails the Arena or triggers an Apoptosis (\fBSTATE_HALT\fR) via the \fBritchie-interlock(2)\fR is strictly inhibited from entering the Live Ingress. Evolution requires survival.
